Z||000000||zeusrekning||03-26-2001||12:36 PM||||Well, thought it was a big dog wanting to race with me in the 88 but... <BR>Deer wiped out the windshild and pass. window. How hard is it to change. I'm assuming the pass window isn't that difficult but not sure about a windshield.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||03-26-2001||01:00 PM||||I actually think the side windows are harder to replace than the windshield.....all of those rivets and tight spaces makes it hard to properly line up.  <P>What other damage did the deer do?  Any body damage, etc.?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||03-26-2001||06:39 PM||||No body damage. You'd figuer it would take out the piece going from the hood to the roof , between the windshield and window.But it didn't.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||03-26-2001||09:38 PM||||If you want to replace to door instead of the just the window, I'm about to replace mine, the window is a lil scratches but nothing bad. you can swap your skin off yours onto mine. <P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GoCartGuy||03-27-2001||02:42 AM||||I know how you feel, I hit one earlier this year.  Thank god for insurance, bill was about $1200, but it did alot more damage.<P>Replacing the windshield is easy, once you get all the stuff for it.  Besides the wind shield you need urethane...comes in a tube like caulk (so you need a gun) and cost anywhere from $8-$12, probably need 2-3 tubes.  You'll also need the seal to sit around the glass, not sure on the price of that, and finally you need a "glazing knife" it's the easiest thing to scrape the old stuff off with.<P>As for the passenger window....replace the whole door....sorry but that thing is a pain in the a@@ to get at.  Good luck and be patient.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homer||03-27-2001||03:08 AM||||Check with your local scrap yard, I just found a windshield in perfect condition all tinted and everything for $45 bucks...man what a steal, the passenger window was like $25<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rocketmad.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||zeusrekning||03-27-2001||03:12 AM||||I have a parts car. I was afraid of how hard it would be to change the windshield.Now i feel it will be removing the door panels. I also need to find some new mirrors. (for the doors) anyone found some cool ones?<BR> Homer?? The front windshield was tinted?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||03-27-2001||11:28 AM||||Umm...  I know things are cramped in the door, but wouldn't it be easier just to remove whatever is left of the side glass and install the new glass?  Just need a hammer, punch, drill, and borrow a "big mamma" rivet gun.  While your at it, and glass is out, replace the dew strip if need be.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||03-27-2001||01:58 PM||||buy a used glass for the door. My windshield shop only charges $115.00 for brand new windshield and they come and install it. Only other charge is if they have to replace the black molding.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||03-27-2001||02:36 PM||||Check with your insurance company. If you have "comprehensive" on your policy, chances are they will buy you a new windshield and wave the deductible. I just had mine replaced and it cost me nothing!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>By the way, I'll the the hind quarter. :razz: I love Bambi meat!<BR>||||reg||3
